========================================
             TESTNG - DATAPROVIDER
========================================

DataProvider is a method in TestNG.

It is used to pass multiple sets of test data to a test method.

Rules to Follow and Remember:

1. A DataProvider method is denoted by @DataProvider annotation.

2. A DataProvider method must return test data.
   Therefore, we need to use the return statement.

3. Generally, we use a 2-dimensional array because we
   usually pass multiple values for each test.

   Example:
   username + password

   Therefore, we commonly use:

   Object[][]

----------------------------------------
SYNTAX:
----------------------------------------

@DataProvider(name = "Dp1")
public Object[][] dataProviderMethod1() {

    Object[][] data = {
        {"username1", "password1"},
        {"username2", "password2"},
        {"username3", "password3"}
    };

    return data;
}

----------------------------------------
HOW IT WORKS:
----------------------------------------

Each row represents ONE set of test data.

Row 1 → username1, password1
Row 2 → username2, password2
Row 3 → username3, password3

So TestNG will execute the test method 3 times.

